payload.description:
Implement story `plx-22c9d5` without changing the default lightweight sandbox behavior.

Bounded scope:
- define an explicit sandbox opt-in and a sanitized, collision-safe sandbox environment namespace;
- reuse a shared non-production VPC/ECR foundation rather than provisioning one VPC per sandbox;
- deploy sandbox-owned queue, dispatcher, ECS service, IAM, alarms, and bindings against the sandbox Task table and AppSync API;
- require an immutable image digest and prohibit production secrets/configuration;
- preserve the audited action authority manifest, one authoritative Task, real executor-owned TaskStages, conditional claim/fencing, cancellation, and image replacement safety;
- ensure sandbox deletion removes only sandbox-owned application resources;
- add executable behavior and focused synthesis/contract coverage before production edits;
- document opt-in, image build/handoff, teardown, cost, and failure behavior.

Out of scope: production deployment, staging promotion proof, extended-duration procedure proof, per-sandbox VPC/ECR foundations, static credentials, fallback dispatchers, a second lifecycle store, and unrelated scoring/container-hardening work.

Return for manager review before commit or deployment: red/green evidence, actual diff, resource/authority counts, exact local validation, proposed commit boundary, and a bounded live sandbox proof plan.
